		"Synth engines",
		"External MIDI sequencing",
		"Performance modes",
		"USB MIDI",
		"TRS MIDI"
	],
	"hardwareControls": [
		"16 by 8 sequencer grid",
		"Four columns of track controls",
		"Parameter encoders"
	],
	"notice": "This is Play+, not the original Play. Configure MIDI input/output, channels and clock routing in the MIDI settings. The grid is shared between sequencing, performance and note-entry functions; no fixed grid note map is assumed. Use the supplied MIDI adapter rather than assuming a TRS wiring standard. Exact browser MIDI port aliases have not been verified; select this profile manually. DIN-connected hardware appears under the MIDI interface name. Physical controls are unbound and this profile does not supply a complete MIDI implementation. Diagrams show selected physical controls with illustrative positions; consult the linked manufacturer references for the full panel.",
